WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:01.756
Switch machines.

2
00:00:02.271 --> 00:00:03.430
Keep your coding history.

3
00:00:04.347 --> 00:00:07.940
Mem Maestro syncs your agent's original sessions and memory

4
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.729
through a private GitHub repository or your Google Drive.

5
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.125
It follows the project's Git remote,

6
00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:15.983
even when the folder path changes.

7
00:00:16.481 --> 00:00:18.026
Start your agent to sync,

8
00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.236
or use the optional Git push and pull hooks.

9
00:00:21.783 --> 00:00:26.996
Claude Code, Codex, Copilot CLI, and Pi are supported,

10
00:00:27.172 --> 00:00:27.991
with Pi in beta.

11
00:00:28.506 --> 00:00:29.609
Need more disk space?

12
00:00:30.065 --> 00:00:33.586
Measure what's stored, then preview old Claude sessions.

13
00:00:33.984 --> 00:00:36.725
Close Claude and archive the sessions you choose

14
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:39.002
to your private GitHub repository.

15
00:00:39.526 --> 00:00:41.553
Mem Maestro uploads the archive,

16
00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:44.433
downloads it again, and verifies every file

17
00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:46.231
before removing local copies.

18
00:00:46.754 --> 00:00:49.960
Existing Git clones and history stay in place.

19
00:00:50.611 --> 00:00:51.948
Need that conversation again?

20
00:00:52.413 --> 00:00:55.666
Restore the original session, then resume in Claude.

21
00:00:56.037 --> 00:00:58.323
Set up Mem Maestro on each machine.

22
00:00:58.766 --> 00:01:00.556
Your history follows your project.

23
00:01:00.884 --> 00:01:03.066
Old sessions stay recoverable.
